        <mxCell id="oe15" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="o_redis" target="o_recsvc">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oe15l" value="feed IDs (~1 ms)" style="edgeLabel;html=1;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="oe15"><mxGeometry x="0" relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oe16" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="o_recsvc" target="o_hydrate">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oe16l" value="20 IDs → multi-get" style="edgeLabel;html=1;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="oe16"><mxGeometry x="0" relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oe17" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="o_hydrate" target="o_gw">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oe17l" value="hydrated items" style="edgeLabel;html=1;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="oe17"><mxGeometry x="0" relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oe18" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="o_gw" target="o_reader">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oe18l" value="GET /v1/recommendations" style="edgeLabel;html=1;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="oe18"><mxGeometry x="0" relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <!-- Trade-offs -->
        <mxCell id="o_to_hdr" value="4 · KEY TRADE-OFFS (each vs a NAMED alternative)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#7030A0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="3050" width="800" height="30" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="o_to" value="Kafka as the pipeline backbone  vs  a cron querying the event DB&#10;    A database is not a stream. &quot;All events in the last 3 min&quot; has no partition key, so it degenerates to scatter-gather over&#10;    every partition. Kafka gives an ordered, offset-addressable, replayable log. Cost: an extra system, and at-least-once&#10;    delivery that the consumer must make idempotent.&#10;&#10;Key events by sessionId  vs  by userId&#10;    Co-view pairs are a within-session, cross-user signal. Keying by userId puts the two halves of a co-view pair on&#10;    different partitions. Cost: per-user aggregation now needs a shuffle or a second keyed stream.&#10;&#10;Regenerate only DIRTY users  vs  regenerate all 100M every 3 min&#10;    Full regeneration = 100M / 180 s ≈ 550k model invocations/s. Infeasible and mostly wasted — the vast majority of users&#10;    are not online. Dirty-only ≈ 180k users per window ≈ 1k/s (10k/s at peak). Cost: a user whose feed drivers changed&#10;    for other reasons (price drop, restock) goes stale — handled by TTL + nightly refresh.&#10;&#10;Two-stage candidate-generation → ranking  vs  ranking the whole catalog&#10;    You cannot score 50M products per request. Cheap recall (ANN + co-view + trending) narrows to ~1–2k, then the&#10;    expensive model ranks only those. Cost: anything recall misses can never be recommended.&#10;&#10;Precompute feeds  vs  compute on read&#10;    p99 200 ms cannot contain candidate generation + model inference. Precompute the top-500, re-rank the top-20&#10;    cheaply at read time with in-session events. Cost: 200 GB of feed storage for users who may never log in — TTL it.&#10;&#10;KV store for feeds  vs  SQL with an index on userId&#10;    Access is a single-key lookup of a blob. No joins, no transactions, no range scans. SQL adds a query planner,&#10;    connection limits and a scaling ceiling for nothing. Cost: no ad-hoc querying of feeds.&#10;&#10;Write-through on generation  vs  cache-aside with CDC invalidation&#10;    The feed generator is the ONLY writer, so it can populate the cache directly — no CDC pipeline, no invalidate-then-&#10;    read race. Cost: cache writes on the generation path. (Cache-aside + coalescing remains right for the long tail.)&#10;&#10;Session cookie + deviceId for anonymous  vs  IP address&#10;    CGNAT collapses thousands of unrelated users behind one IP, and mobile IPs change mid-session — so IP both&#10;    merges strangers' co-views and splits one person's session. Cost: cookie loss = lost identity; accept it." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#BF9000;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="3085" width="1160" height="640" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- Deep dives -->
        <mxCell id="o_dd_hdr" value="5 · DEEP DIVES" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#7030A0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1240" y="3050" width="800" height="30" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="o_dd" value="THE CORE HARD PROBLEM — co-view at 100k events/s&#10;    Flink sessionizes by sessionId (session gap 30 min), emits pairs (A,B) for products co-viewed in a session.&#10;    A session of k views yields k² pairs — cap k (last 20 viewed) or pairs will blow up on crawler-like sessions.&#10;    Aggregate counts in a sliding window, then normalise: raw counts just re-rank the catalog by popularity.&#10;    Use lift / PMI — count(A,B) / (count(A)·count(B)) — so &quot;phone case&quot; doesn't recommend &quot;iPhone&quot; to everyone.&#10;&#10;WHERE IT BREAKS AT SCALE&#10;    Break 1 — full feed regeneration: 550k inferences/s. Fix: dirty-user-only + TTL, → ~1k/s, 10k/s at peak.&#10;    Break 2 — cron over Cassandra: scatter-gather over every partition per window. Fix: Kafka log, offset-addressed.&#10;    Break 3 — co-view pair explosion: cap session length, count-min sketch for the tail, exact counts for the head.&#10;    Break 4 — 10x peak on reads (30k homepage + 100k pdp /s): CDN the /similar endpoint (public, not personalized) —&#10;                     that removes most of the pdp load before it reaches the service.&#10;&#10;HOT KEYS / HOT PARTITIONS&#10;    A viral product's ItemSimilarity key is read by every visitor on that pdp. Redis: replicate as key#0..key#N and&#10;    pick at random; plus a short-TTL in-process local cache in the service. Kafka: a bot session can hot-spot one&#10;    partition — cap per-session throughput at ingest.&#10;&#10;CONSISTENCY &amp; IDEMPOTENCY&#10;    Kafka is at-least-once, so co-view counts double-count on replay. Dedup by eventId in the window, or write&#10;    absolute aggregates rather than increments. Feeds are eventually consistent by design — but pagination must be&#10;    stable, so the cursor pins feedVersion and a regeneration mid-scroll doesn't shuffle page 2.&#10;&#10;OPERABILITY — how you know it is stale or wrong&#10;    • Feed staleness histogram: now − generatedAt, p50/p99. Alert when p99 &gt; 3 min (that IS the SLA).&#10;    • Kafka consumer lag per partition — the leading indicator; staleness is the lagging one.&#10;    • Coverage: % of DAU with a fresh feed. Fallback rate: % of responses with isFallback=true.&#10;    • Empty/short-response rate, out-of-stock leakage rate, CTR as a guardrail against a bad model version.&#10;    • Model version pinned per feed row so a bad rollout is attributable and revertible.&#10;&#10;FAILURE MODES&#10;    Redis down → KV store (slower, survivable). KV down → trending/popular fallback, isFallback=true.&#10;    Flink down → feeds stale but served; alert on staleness, replay from Kafka offsets on recovery.&#10;    Ranking service down → serve the previous feed; it is a recommendation, not a payment.&#10;&#10;COLD START&#10;    New user: popular-in-category + geo trending, personalise after the first few events.&#10;    New product: content-based similarity from title/category/embedding until co-view data accrues." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;fillColor=#F8CECC;strokeColor=#B85450;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1240" y="3085" width="1140" height="760" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
